The ONLY place ordered_at is stamped is applyLifecycle (line 102: `if (rank >= RANK.po_sent && !current?.ordered_at && !upd.ordered_at) upd.ordered_at = nowIso;`), which is invoked solely from the PATCH /items/:id route (line 179) — NOT from issue-po. captureLeadObservation then bails when ordered_at is missing: procurementLearningService.mjs:32 `if (!item.supplier_id || !item.ordered_at || !item.delivered_at) return null;`.

draft-po sets the PO total from allowance as a fallback (procurementRoutes.mjs:371): `const amount = Number(item.approved_amount ?? item.quoted_amount ?? item.cost_allowance ?? 0) || 0;` and only requires `amount > 0` (line 374). But computeCommittedCost deliberately excludes cost_allowance:
  if ((STATUS_RANK[it.status] ?? 0) >= RANK_PO_SENT) {
