PUT /api/templates/:key/content upserts the DB row with hardcoded catalog values:
```
const payload = {
  catalog_key: entry.key, module: entry.module, category: entry.category || null,
  title: entry.title, kind: entry.kind, storage: "dropbox", storage_path: path,
  edit_method: "Edit in Hub (writes the .md master to Dropbox)", status: entry.status || "active",
  purpose: entry.purpose || null, version: (existing?.version || 1) + (existing ? 1 : 0),
  updated_at: new Date().toISOString(),
};
if (existing) await sb.from("document_templates").update(payload).eq("id", existing.id);
```
The payload always uses `entry.*` (the in-code catalog), and `update()` is a full overwrite of every key in `payload`. This directly contradicts the documented contract in templateCatalog.mjs:172 (`Merge the code catalogue with DB override rows ... DB wins per-field`) and mergeCatalogWithRows (templateCatalog.mjs:173-188), which lets PATCH-set DB values override the catalog.

v2 client financial snapshot counts a client-acknowledged-but-not-yet-signed variation as APPROVED and folds it into the contract total:
```
const clientApproved = decByVar[v.id] === "approved";
if (v.status === "signed" || v.status === "invoiced" || clientApproved) snapshot.approvedVariations += amt;
